From: Rungic <noreply@rungic.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: Android host: initialize Linux desktop before the first display connection

Keep one configured phone output with its render loop inhibited when no Android
host exists at startup. Open Linux's render device independently, defer host
windows and layers, and use the existing reconnect path to attach presentation.
The ordinary nested Wayland backend still requires its upstream compositor.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-06
X-Rungic-Status: Pending
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:session.ready
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/113
Origin: vendor
---
diff --git a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_backend.h b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_backend.h
--- a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_backend.h
+++ b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_backend.h
@@ -291,6 +291,8 @@
     void removeOutput(WaylandOutput *output);
     /// Settings of the host connection before it is made.
     virtual void configureDisplay(WaylandDisplay *display);
+    /// Android presentation can be absent on the very first Linux boot.
+    virtual bool allowOfflineStart() const { return false; }
     /// The render device to open: the host's dmabuf main device upstream.
     virtual QString renderDevicePath() const;
     /// Called once the render device is open (e.g. to give it another allocator).
